Reviewing the eight remaining -k repository_artifact_matches_deterministic_replay
failures found only three are the fabrication-gate-stamp cause (exp5342/5368/
5383). Four are stale-receipt residue the 2026-08-25 adoption (64846b5430) was
meant to remove: exp5412/5425/5438/5451 still hashed the shared KAN spec from
the working tree, and that spec last changed 2026-07-14, six days after their
artifacts landed. The eighth, exp5736, records live machine state
(disk_free_mb), the residual cause 64846b5430 already named.

Why the sweep missed them: it enumerated "replay-tested modules" by the literal
assertion `result == replay`. The four KAN tests assert `checked_in == replay`.
A pattern list narrower than its concept, inside the sweep that was checking
for that class — the same failure shape that commit already confessed for its
first helper-name grep. The spec's Implementation Status carries the appended
correction.

The change per module is the established two-line adoption: import
receipt_bytes/receipt_exists and route _sha256_if_exists through them, pinned
to RESULT_RELATIVE_PATH's add-commit. Receipts over upstream results/ paths
keep reading the working tree per REQ-REPORT-6610-EVIDENCE-LIVE. ruff format
reflowed the four files; the semantic change per module is the import plus one
helper body, same cost 64846b5430 paid and recorded.

Proofs, in a PYTHONPATH-pinned git worktree with the interpreter's import file
verified against the worktree before every reading:

  four replay tests RED before adoption, GREEN after (33/33 in the four files)
  tampered recorded spec hash                        -> RED, restored
  dropped dependency key from the recorded receipt   -> RED, restored
  flagged_adversarial added to upstream exp5406      -> RED, restored
    (the EVIDENCE-LIVE working-tree read survived adoption; a gate stamp on
     evidence still moves these receipts)
  flagged_adversarial dropped from exp5342, staged   -> determination
    preservation lint REFUSES, and refuses the true->false flip too

The -k selection moves 8 failed / 49 passed to 4 failed / 53 passed. The four
still red assert a contract the fabrication-gate discipline forbids from
holding (post-hoc stamps on exp5342/5368/5383; live disk_free_mb on exp5736).
Changing what those REQs assert is an operator decision and is escalated in
the review report, not patched here. The test_experiment_6659_v580_capstone
errors are a live-roadmap coupling (expects milestone 2026.08.580, roadmap is
at .582) — the REQ-REPORT-6610-SCOPE parsed-content class recurring in a new
capstone, recorded in ops/changelog.md.

